From: Amphoze <184834775+Amphoze@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 09:49:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] query: the record of what is sent to a project's database

One line per statement or type generation, in a file of the project on the server's data
volume: the time, the project, who asked and in which role, the login used, the kind, and for
a statement the SHA-256 of its text. The line is JSON with a fixed order of members, so no
value can end a line or add a member; it is refused when its reader would not take it. It is
appended and flushed before its writer returns, one write at a time per project; a line that
would take the file past its bound moves the file to a single older generation first. When
the line is not on the volume the writer throws 503 audit_unavailable.
